# Negative-control mutant — contract-product staged-import guard (AC-11)
#
# RE-TARGETED (this pass): the guard moved out of the deleted `selectStatusNode`
#   util and now lives in the machine's `loading.invoke.onDone` entry order, as
#   the first arm `{ target: STAGED, cond: "isStaged" }`. The mutation and the
#   break are unchanged; only the site moved.
#
# Scenario it must flip: contract-product.feature >
#   "A product still being imported cannot be changed"
# Test that goes red: contract-product.mutations.int.test.ts >
#   "AC-11 a staged product refuses stopRenewing and setConsolidation, sending no request to either endpoint"
#   (a staged row now lands on its raw `status.code` node — `available.status.active`
#   — so STOP_RENEWING and SET_CONSOLIDATION enter `processing` and a request is
#   observed against `.../modify_renew` and `.../properties`; both `toEqual([])` flip).
# Mutation: `loading.invoke.onDone` drops its `isStaged` arm, so a staged import
#   is placed by its raw `status.code` alone — the protection is gone.
#
# THE SECOND MUTATION THAT COMMENT NAMES — DISCLOSED, NOT DROPPED.
#   `contract-product.feature`'s AC-11 mutant comment names TWO mutations:
#   removing the staged-import protection (this patch) and withholding the
#   same changes from a merely SUSPENDED subscription. The second has a
#   POSITIVE control — "A suspended subscription is still offered every
#   change" is driven per row on the wire by
#   contract-product.mutations.int.test.ts — but no mutant of its own, and it
#   is not authored, for one cause: the behaviour it protects is the ABSENCE
#   of a refusal. There is no guard to delete. A patch would have to INVENT a
#   suspended-state refusal and then remove it, which grades the patch rather
#   than the module — the same misrepresentation the `delegated-preference`
#   filename was pulled for. Stated here so the comment's second limb is a
#   disclosed withholding, never an un-met promise.
#
# Apply with:  git apply <this file>   (run from repo root)
# Revert with: git apply -R <this file>
diff --git a/packages/headless/src/modules/contract-product/contract-product.machine.ts b/packages/headless/src/modules/contract-product/contract-product.machine.ts
